<title>GERMANY: German 1996 average numbers in work dip 1.2 pct.</title>
<headline>German 1996 average numbers in work dip 1.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN NUMBERS IN WORK	  1996    1995     Pct change</p>
<p> Number in work (unadj, million)   34.504  34.909    -1.2</p>
<p>WEST GERMAN</p>
<p> Number in work (unadj,million)    28.215  28.523    -1.1</p>
<p>EAST GERMAN</p>
<p> Number in work (unadj, million)    6.289   6.386    -1.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are provisional and unadjusted and refer to people working in the respective regions but not necessarily living in Germany.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
